However, looking more carefully at the `wordsNeeded` function, I think there might be a more subtle issue. Let me examine it again:

```go
func wordsNeeded(i uint) int {
	if i > (Cap() - wordMask) {
		return int(Cap() >> log2WordSize)
	}
	return int((i + wordMask) >> log2WordSize)
}
```

The issue might be in the condition `i > (Cap() - wordMask)`. When `i` is very close to `Cap()`, `Cap() - wordMask` might not behave as expected due to integer arithmetic properties.

